= Introduction <introduction>


There is a well-established discrepancy between transcriptomic and proteomic measurements, whereby only approximately 40% of the variation observed at the protein level can be explained by corresponding mRNA expression levels @vogel2012. Although proteins are synthesized from transcripts and both ultimately originate from the genomic blueprint, multiple regulatory layers—including translational control and protein degradation—contribute to this divergence @crick1970.


This discrepancy may pose a significant challenge for biomedical research aimed at glioblastoma multiforme (GBM), the most aggressive form of brain tumor, which historically already has poor survivability @lemee2018, as it creates an unclear target for GBM medicine research. Combined with the increase in AI-driven methods based on transciptomic and proteomic data obtained from GBM @singh2022, clarity regarding the understand of the data is of important interest.  

The content of this thesis aims to statistically compare and contrast transcriptomics and proteomics of GBM via differential analysis of their respective expression data against healthy brain tissue.

Chapter @background presents the relevant knowledge regarding the thesis's topic, including the biological entity of interest - glioblastoma, and multiomics.